			"Message": "feat(Land): Gate asset deployment strategy behind $TierSchemeAssets env var\n\nSwitch the default TierSchemeAssets from Embedded to FileSystem in the sample .env file, and advance both the Element and Dependency submodules to pull in the matching infrastructure.\n\nThe Element submodule advances to 0211d129, bringing Mountain's build-time gating mechanism that reads $TierSchemeAssets (defaulting to \"Embedded\") and mutates tauri.conf.json to select between Embedded (Brotli-compressed, self-contained binary) and FileSystem (disk layout served via localhost plugin static_root) deployment modes. build.rs conditionally sets frontendDist, bundle.resources, and the file-system static_root fallback code is gated behind #[cfg(feature = \"TierSchemeAssetsFileSystem\")].\n\nThe Dependency submodule advances to 4ecfadfd, incorporating the latest VS Code Editor upstream fixes and Tauri v2.11.2 with Android build toolchain fixes, Tao 0.35.2, Wry 0.55.1, and Brotli content encoding support.\n\nMaking FileSystem the default in the sample config optimises the development workflow for fast rebuild cycles, while Embedded remains the release-build default through the build.rs fallback — zero-config safety for production.",
			"SHA": "66cdf7af878503c52308aaeb2b6170b5a730c24a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T08:22:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Land): Advance Element submodule to 9ea79767\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to pull in a coordinated refactor across five submodules that consolidates Mountain's Tauri bundle layout and normalises indentation conventions.\n\nMountain restructures bundle resources under a canonical Static/Application/ prefix, unifying the flat bundle layout (Contents/Resources/extensions) with the monorepo dev layout (Sky/Target/Static/Application/extensions). The tauri.conf.json remaps all resource entries, sets frontendDist to null for dev-server delegation, and LocalhostPlugin.rs gains static_root resolution that probes both production and dev bundle paths. ScanPathConfigure.rs registers the new canonical path before legacy flat fallbacks.\n\nCocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker align their ESBuild configuration files and compiled artifacts to project-wide tab-based indentation, trailing commas, import-before-declaration ordering, and consolidated export blocks.\n\nZero functional changes across the five submodules — flat-path fallbacks in Mountain preserve existing dev environments and CI compatibility during the migration.",
			"SHA": "74411523d579d111a52e2f7ff82f512a46e1b45d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T07:33:54Z",
